 (:calendar "MW" :key "cap-18-05" :from (1967 7 28) :to nil
  :authority "Public Holidays Act, Chapter 18:05 (Act 11 of 1967), revised and consolidated to 31 December 2014 (L.R.O. 1/2015)"
  :uri "https://web.archive.org/web/20211202034241id_/https://malawilii.org/akn/mw/act/1967/11/eng@2014-12-31"
  :issued (1967 7 28) :issued-uri "https://malawilii.org/akn/mw/act/1967/11/eng@2014-12-31" :published nil :published-in "Laws of Malawi, Fourth Revised Edition (L.R.O. 1/2015), via MalawiLII" :in-force (1967 7 28) :dates-note "Commencement 28 July 1967 per MalawiLII; the 1967 Gazette issue was not located." :summary "s.2 Schedule days are public holidays. s.3(1) the Minister may amend the Schedule by Gazette order; s.3(2) may declare any day a public holiday (in addition or in substitution, nationally or locally). s.4 [16 of 1983]: where a Schedule day other than the Saturday following Good Friday falls on a Saturday or Sunday, the next succeeding day not being itself a Sunday or public holiday is the public holiday and the Schedule day ceases to be one. Schedule (as amended by G.N. 99/1986, 67/1994, 84/1994, 76/1997, 41/2007): New Year's Day; John Chilembwe Day (15 January); Martyrs' Day (3 March); Good Friday; Saturday following Good Friday; Easter Monday; Labour Day (1 May); Kamuzu Day (14 May); Independence Day (6 July); Mothers' Day (15 October); Eid al Fitri; Christmas Day. NO Boxing Day in the Schedule.")
 (:calendar "MW" :key "gn-41-2007" :from nil :to nil
  :authority "Government Notice 41 of 2007 (last amendment of the Schedule)"
  :uri "https://web.archive.org/web/20211202034241id_/https://malawilii.org/akn/mw/act/1967/11/eng@2014-12-31"
  :issued nil :published nil :published-in "Malawi Gazette, 2007" :in-force nil :dates-note "Known only from the amendment list under the Schedule; text not found." :summary "Content unknown. Secondary sources: the Mutharika government restored Kamuzu Day (14 May, dropped under Muluzi, who had a Freedom Day on 14 June) and delisted Boxing Day; reports differ between 2007 and 2009 for the Kamuzu Day restoration. The earlier G.N.s 67/1994, 84/1994, 76/1997 are the Muluzi-era changes (contents not seen; possibly John Chilembwe Day, Freedom Day and Eid al-Fitr).")
